WEBVTT

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.010
The Trigger of Memories

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:00.720
<i>The news of the devastation of Whitechurch</i>

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.340
<i>shook the citizens as much as the previous war.</i>

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.570
<i>But, two weeks later,</i>

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:10.760
<i>another major incident occurred 
that would shake them to the core.</i>

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.800
There was a time when our nation of Patria

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.370
fought divided between 
the North and the South.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:19.350
But what came of that?

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:22.000
Absolutely nothing! Not one thing changed!

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:26.440
Even now, the filthy rich and the 
incompetent nobles of the North,

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.870
as well as both governments, which are 
now nothing more than puppets...

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:35.500
These old rulers are suffocating 
this country and making us suffer!

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.720
My fellow citizens, 
who wish for true equality...

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.080
Now is the time to rise up!

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.880
Overcome the border between North and South,

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.960
and create a new world together!

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:50.000
Along with us Incarnates!

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:55.520
In this moment, I declare 
the birth of New Patria!

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:02.030
<i>Together with the soldiers and nobles who 
were unsatisfied with the war's ending,</i>

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.030
<i>as well as some of the citizens,</i>

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.700
<i>Cain Madhouse and the Incarnates established</i>

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:11.540
<i>their independence from 
their motherland of Patria.</i>

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.990
<i>They built their base in the west, 
which had lagged behind in development,</i>

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:20.880
<i>and began to grow as one city after 
another decided to align with them.</i>

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:25.470
<i>Meanwhile, the government of 
the Northern Union of Patria,</i>

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:30.120
<i>where the scars from the 
previous war had yet to heal,</i>

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:33.550
<i>decided to prepare their 
defenses for the upcoming war.</i>

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:38.020
<i>The government was fearful that 
the Incarnates who remained</i>

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:42.400
<i>in the North would soon join the rebel 
forces and, after a conference,</i>

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.790
<i>they decided to annihilate any 
Incarnates remaining in the land.</i>

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:53.120
<i>Silently, but surely,</i>

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:57.140
<i>the giant footsteps of war 
were drawing nearer...</i>

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.570
It's so cold...

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.560
Sch... Schaal!

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:27.870
It's been six months. How have you been?

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:31.030
Huh? Er, uh, um...

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:33.800
I'm happy to... see you again...

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:44.010
<i>I never thought I'd be able 
to come back here again.</i>

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.450
<i>Back then, the bullet that 
should've gone through me</i>

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:52.780
<i>was stopped by the dress I was wearing.</i>

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:57.210
<i>Apparently the dress was made with special 
cloth woven from an Incarnate's thread.</i>

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:03.870
<i>I still have no idea why they 
had me wear such a dress.</i>

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:09.880
<i>I survived, but what awaited me 
was an interrogation by the military.</i>

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:14.490
<i>The military had stripped Hank of his rank 
after what he did at Whitechurch,</i>

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:16.640
<i>and they were searching for him.</i>

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:17.660
<i>However...</i>

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.190
I'm home...

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.140
Father.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:30.820
I guess this place never changes.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:34.000
It feels as though I only 
left this town yesterday.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.900
I met some of the people
 you fought alongside.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:47.560
I saw the burden you had 
to bear with my own eyes.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.810
I originally left this town to get revenge,

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.350
but the more I find out,

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:57.040
the less I know what to believe.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:01.750
I'm not exactly sure...

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.710
what I want to do with him.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:10.080
Father... please...

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:22.400
Schaal? Schaal, it's you!

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:24.160
Liza?

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.310
What in the world are you doing here?

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:30.280
I was born in this town. 
What brings you here, Liza?

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.940
I'm working with this squad right now.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:34.690
The reason we came here is...

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:36.090
An Incarnate?

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:39.830
Yes. There's someone who ran 
into one in these mountains.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:43.970
We're about to go into the mountains 
and eliminate the Incarnate.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.250
I-I beg of you...

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:48.340
Please, get rid of it!

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.290
E-Excuse me...

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:56.380
Would you allow me to go with you?

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:57.600
Schaal!

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.200
Schaal...

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.200
You're...

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:02.290
Nancy Schaal Bancroft.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:07.620
I read your file. You were 
traveling with Hank Henriette.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.880
She's from this town.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:13.100
I asked her to guide us, since she's 
knowledgeable about the area.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:17.200
Plus, she won't freak out 
if she sees an Incarnate.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.340
Who could ask for a better guide?

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.620
I see.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:23.330
It's true that it'll be easier to find our target

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.630
if we're with someone who knows the area.

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:31.370
All right. Very well.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:51.220
Have some. It'll warm you up.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:53.780
Th-Thank you.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:03.070
I'm very sorry we let such 
a thing happen to you.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:08.060
Even though we were there at Whitechurch, 
there were many casualties.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.590
I'm glad you survived that hellish scene.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:15.800
Wait, did you come here to tell me that?

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:21.480
Jeez, you're too serious for your own good.

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:26.600
I can't control my urge 
to tease little boys like you.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.690
It's just too irresistible.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.870
Take that... and that, and that.

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:34.600
Second Lieute—

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.780
My, aren't you bold?!

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:40.040
Did you want to have a different 
kind of tussle with me out here?

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.080
I won't lose to a little boy like you!

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:49.570
Second Lieutenant Liza Renecastle... 
I'm your commander!

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:51.050
Stop this at once!

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:54.230
Oh, I know, Major Claude.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:56.130
Huh? Major?

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.700
He's young, but he shot right up the ranks.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.210
Although he's also a bit special...

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:05.380
considering he's the son of 
this country's president.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:06.010
Huh?

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.600
I know the rank I've been 
given is well above my means.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:15.690
But since I've been given this mission,
 I intend to complete it, no matter the cost.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:20.820
As the leader of Coup de Grâce, 
I will eliminate every last Incarnate!

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.480
They should not exist in this 
country... no, this world!

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:27.140
For any reason!

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:35.780
What's that?

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.140
It's coming from over there!

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.760
An Incarnate!

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:58.440
Hey!

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:03.120
Why... What are you doing here...

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:05.740
Father?!

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.210
Father...

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:17.300
What the...

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.090
Its flesh is rotting...

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.770
Father...

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:30.380
Look out!

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:36.140
No...

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:40.850
Fire!

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:55.860
Halt!

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.310
There's no need to pursue it.

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:01.090
We won't be able to finish it 
with our current firepower.

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:04.430
Father... Why?

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:12.480
The Incarnate that attacked us is Nidhogg.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:15.570
His name when he was in the army 
was John William Bancroft.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:17.440
Bancroft?

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:21.060
Yes. That's her father.

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:23.460
I see.

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:25.550
According to our records,

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:29.420
Nidhogg was shot and killed by Hank, 
and its corpse was buried by the military.

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:34.360
So an Incarnate that was supposed 
to be dead rose from its grave?

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:38.170
There are some Incarnates with an 
incredible amount of life force.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:43.380
Somehow, its corpse must have been 
revitalized and started moving again.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.650
It's completely lost its humanity.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:51.310
We need to eliminate it at once 
before there are any casualties.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.340
Once preparations are complete,

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:58.680
we will carry out our mission to
 eliminate the Incarnate, Nidhogg!

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.040
Hurry!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.600
Put some of the bombs over there, too!

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:20.600
What kind of father was he?

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:25.680
He was a very calm, gentle man.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.500
He rarely ever got mad.

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:33.130
He was always kind and looked after 
me and the children at the orphanage.

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:38.640
He was the last person you could picture 
fighting, let alone becoming a soldier.

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:40.390
And yet...

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:44.110
I have the power to help end this war

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:48.110
and make sure that you and the other 
kids can live happily in the future.

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:51.750
This is my time to pull the trigger.

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:56.980
And then he left for the 
battlefield... for our sakes.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:00.600
Then, when he came home...

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:11.260
He may have looked different, 
but he was still my father.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:13.230
Schaal...

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:17.620
You should head back to town. 
It's best you stay away from here.

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:19.930
Why?

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.290
I must face anything, however difficult, 
without running away.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:26.360
I know that's what my father would do.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:30.310
So... I don't want to run away, either.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:32.690
I see.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.630
In that case, hang on to this.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:41.560
These are...

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:44.160
Yes, they're Godkiller bullets.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:48.380
We don't know what might happen, 
so I'll give those to you, just in case.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:10.150
It's coming!

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:11.570
Father...

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:13.120
Commence attack!

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:41.230
Fall back!

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:16.760
It can't be...

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.220
That direction is...

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:25.600
Father, no!

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:27.300
Our town is over there!

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:29.850
Second Lieutenant! Head back to the town!

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.420
Evacuate the people there!

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:33.350
We'll slow it down!

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.580
Got it!

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:45.170
Fall back, Gerald.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:46.330
I'll take care of it!

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:21.540
Everyone, please run!

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:23.740
Don't you know what time it is?

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:25.050
Who is that?

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:26.200
It's Schaal...

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:26.750
What's going on?

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.190
Please, hurry!

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:30.170
Everyone, you need to evacuate at once!

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.310
Hurry!

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:33.070
Give us a break already.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:35.610
Schaal, did you bring us trouble ag—

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:37.460
What's that?

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:43.470
Will!

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:44.230
N-No way!

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.220
I thought he died!

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:50.730
What are you doing?! Hurry up and run!

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:52.400
Please, don't...

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:56.060
Get out of here, you monster!

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:03.140
This is my time to pull the trigger.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.780
What are you doing?! Run!

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:07.520
Hurry!

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:08.930
Wait, Schaal!

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.120
What is she doing? Does she want to die?!

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:24.040
<i>On that day, my father 
left for the battlefield</i>

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.630
<i>to protect me, the orphans, 
and everyone in this town.</i>

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:37.030
<i>Now, he has lost his soul and is trying 
to harm those who are precious to him.</i>

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.970
Before they become Beasts...

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:40.920
I must slay them while they're still human.

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:45.200
That's my final duty as the 
Incarnate squad captain.

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:46.730
<i>Right...</i>

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:51.370
<i>That's why Hank is doing this.</i>

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:55.910
<i>In order to protect their wishes from when</i>

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.250
<i>they were still human.</i>

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:03.840
Don't worry. You're a strong girl.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:07.840
When the time comes for you to pull the 
trigger, I know you'll be able to do it.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:09.620
Father!

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:27.750
<i>Please stop.</i>

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:32.530
<i>Please stop...</i>

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:35.690
<i>Please stop!</i>

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:38.590
Schaal...

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:43.130
<i>Please stop...</i>

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:49.220
I'm begging you, please stop!

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.620
Father...

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:16.690
Liza...

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:18.350
You're so reckless, you know that?

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:19.580
I'm sorry.

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:23.850
I just didn't know this whole time...

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:29.990
How my father felt in his last moments 
on the day he was shot by Hank.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:33.400
But now, I understand.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:37.250
Back then, I'm sure my father...

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:45.440
I was finally able to say goodbye to my father.

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:47.490
Schaal...

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.410
Huh? Huh?!

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:53.600
Hush, now.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:20:59.220
<i>But...</i>

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.690
<i>Still, I can't help but wonder</i>

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:05.240
<i>if there really is no other way...</i>

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:11.120
<i>If their only salvation is 
their burial, then Hank...</i>

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:19.150
Liza, I have a request.

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:53.220
Are you serious?

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:56.140
Yes. I want us to bring her along.

00:22:56.450 --> 00:22:58.870
I want to see Hank.

00:22:58.870 --> 00:23:01.050
I have something I need to say to him!

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:06.230
Second Lieutenant, you know 
how grave our mission is.

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:10.250
We're grateful for her help, 
but we can't ask for—

00:23:10.250 --> 00:23:13.450
We don't know the current 
whereabouts of Hank Henriette,

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:18.390
but if you come with us, we're bound 
to run into him sooner or later.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:21.580
I will allow you to accompany us.

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:24.240
Yes, sir!

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:26.920
Everyone calls me Trice.

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:27.870
A singer?!

00:23:27.870 --> 00:23:30.220
She seems like a girl 
you'd find in any town.

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:33.000
When are they coming?

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:35.930
You're not going to listen 
to my song either, are you?

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:38.860
Please let me hear your song.

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:40.050
Songstress of Sleep
